      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 4 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $A$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrices  $C$ and $B$ have exactly $3$ pivot columns.  So, $\\text{rank}(C)=\\text{rank}(B)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are \"$C$  and $B$ only.\"",
